body:
## Summary

Canonical, history-free port of the reviewed Azure intake from Yolkster64/helios-platform#1 at `44e6ffb1177d1c962946f2f6b59866d3c80a2197`, rebuilt on current canonical `main` at `bd32f53def6939ceebc48885d5a18e2913fea28d`.

This draft adds only the governed integration slice:

- internal VNet-bound Container Apps design, Premium ACR, Key Vault, Log Analytics, Application Insights, and UAMI;
- containerized read-only Monado status API/GUI;
- explicit unbound Hermes adapter boundary;
- XCore safe standby that cannot be enabled by an environment flag;
- PR-only Bicep/container validation;
- protected `azure-dev` OIDC plan/apply stages with canonical-repository, protected-main, and exact-scope guards;
- sanitized property-level what-if evidence bound to source/template/parameters/runtime IDs, with drift rejection before apply;
- immutable image digest release and post-release ARM verification.

## Deliberate exclusions

- No fork history or synthetic merge commit.
- No `azure.yaml` or default parameter file, so there is no parallel `azd up` path.
- No Bicep role assignment. Exact-registry `AcrPull` must be pre-provisioned by a separately approved identity.
- No public-ingress parameter. Container Apps environment and app ingress are internal-only.
- No Azure environment variables, federation credential, RBAC mutation, live resource creation, or `deploy=true` run.

## Validation completed locally

- Python compilation;
- workflow YAML structure and every shell block;
- all referenced actions pinned to full commit SHAs;
- PR/OIDC/deployment path isolation;
- plan evidence create/verify/compare and sensitive-drift rejection;
- status API, forced-XCore standby, GUI, traversal rejection, and server-header smoke;
- `git diff --check`.

GitHub Actions is authoritative for Bicep compilation and container build because Azure CLI/Bicep/Docker are unavailable in the local workspace.

## Draft blockers

- PR #174 must merge, then this branch must rebase and reconcile resource ownership into the post-#174 canonical enterprise Bicep graph.
- The canonical control-plane subnet must be approved, sized, and delegated.
- ACR/Key Vault private endpoints and DNS, private APIM, Entra authorization, controlled egress, internal runtime verification, rollback evidence, SBOM, signing, and attestation remain required.
- Protected `azure-dev` must remain unconfigured until reviewers, prevent-self-review, disabled admin bypass, main-only branch policy, the canonical federation subject `repo:M0nado/helios-platform:environment:azure-dev`, exact variables, and the custom least-privilege deployment role are approved.

Do not run `deploy=true`.
